/*Q19. A courier company needs to calculate the volume of shipping cartons of different shapes. Design a Java program using constructor
overloading, method overloading, and a static method.
Class: Box
Create a separate class named Box with the following instance variables:
• length (double) — represents the length of the box.
• breadth (double) — represents the breadth of the box.
• height (double) — represents the height of the box.
Constructors
Implement the following overloaded constructors:
• Box() — initializes all three dimensions to 1.0.
• Box(double side) — creates a cube by assigning the given side to all three dimensions.
• Box(double length, double breadth, double height) — initializes the box with the specified dimensions.
Methods
Implement the following methods:
• volume() (double) — returns the volume calculated as length x breadth x height.
• volume(double scaleFactor) (double) — returns the original volume multiplied by the given scale factor.
• static volume(double 1, double b, double h) (double) — returns the volume calculated using the supplied dimensions.
• displayDimensions() (void) — displays the length, breadth, and height of the box, each on a separate line.
Class: BoxDemo
Implement the BoxDemo class to perform the following operations:
1. Create a default Box object.
2. Read the side of a cube and create a cube object.
3. Read the length, breadth, and height of a rectangular box and create its object.
4. Read a scale factor for each box.
5. Display the dimensions, original volume, and scaled volume of each box.
6. Read three additional dimensions and calculate their volume using the static volume() method.
Input Format:
The input consists of the following values, each provided on a separate line:
• Side of the cube — double
• Length of the rectangular box — double
• Breadth of the rectangular box — double
• Height of the rectangular box — double
• Scale factor for the default box — double
• Scale factor for the cube box — double
• Scale factor for the rectangular box — double
• Length for static volume calculation — double
• Breadth for static volume calculation — double
• Height for static volume calculation — double
Output Format:
Display the details of each box:
Default Box:
Length: <length>
Breadth: <breadth>
Height: <height>
Volume: <volume>
Scaled Volume: <scaled_volume>
Cube Box:
Length: <length>
Breadth: <breadth>
Height: <height>
Volume: <volume>
Scaled Volume: <scaled_volume>
Rectangular Box:
Length: <length>
Breadth: <breadth>
Height: <height>
Volume: <volume>
Scaled Volume: <scaled_volume>
Static Volume: <volume>
*/
/////////////////////////////////////////////////

import java.util.Scanner;
 
class Box {
    double length, breadth, height;
 
    Box() {
        this(1.0, 1.0, 1.0);
    }
 
    Box(double side) {
        this(side, side, side);
    }
 
    Box(double length, double breadth, double height) {
        this.length = length;
        this.breadth = breadth;
        this.height = height;
    }
 
    double volume() {
        return length * breadth * height;
    }
 
    double volume(double scaleFactor) {
        return volume() * scaleFactor;
    }
 
    static double volume(double l, double b, double h) {
        return l * b * h;
    }
 
    void displayDimensions() {
        System.out.println("Length: " + length);
        System.out.println("Breadth: " + breadth);
        System.out.println("Height: " + height);
    }
}
 
public class BoxDemo {
    static void show(String label, Box box, double scale) {
        System.out.println(label);
        box.displayDimensions();
        System.out.println("Volume: " + box.volume());
        System.out.println("Scaled Volume: " + box.volume(scale));
    }
 
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        Box defaultBox = new Box();
        double side = sc.nextDouble();
        Box cube = new Box(side);
        double l = sc.nextDouble(), b = sc.nextDouble(), h = sc.nextDouble();
        Box rect = new Box(l, b, h);
        double s1 = sc.nextDouble(), s2 = sc.nextDouble(), s3 = sc.nextDouble();
        double sl = sc.nextDouble(), sb = sc.nextDouble(), sh = sc.nextDouble();
 
        show("Default Box:", defaultBox, s1);
        show("Cube Box:", cube, s2);
        show("Rectangular Box:", rect, s3);
        System.out.println("Static Volume: " + Box.volume(sl, sb, sh));
        sc.close();
    }
}
